/value "-0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412576} :answer-field/id #uuid "dab95909-e45b-53f1-bf4f-61cf81c795fb" :answer-field/key "field-8" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412624}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fbf3d356-bb6f-5d45-9a65-7f6a6ff861ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-221834" :question/problem "Disprove the following statement:\n\n${x}^{2}+5x+6\\ge 0$ for any $x\\in R.$\n\nTo {{field-1}} a universal statement, it's sufficient to find a {{field-2}}. \nIn other words, we need to show that {{field-3}}\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+5x+6{{field-4}}0.\n$$\n\nBy substituting $x=$ {{field-5}} into the expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+5x+6 & ={({{field-6}})}^{2}+5({{field-7}})+6 \\\\  & ={{field-8}} \\\\  & {{field-9}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $x=$ {{field-10}} is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false." :question/worked-solution "Our statement can be written as\n\n$$\n∀x\\in R,\\,{x}^{2}+5x+6\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nWe want to disprove this statement. In other words, we must show that its negation is true:\n\n$$\n¬(∀x\\in R,\\,{x}^{2}+5x+6\\ge 0)\\,≡\\,∃x\\in R,\\,{x}^{2}+5x+6<0\n$$\n\nSo, we begin as follows:\n\nTo disprove a universal statement, it's sufficient to find a counterexample. In other words, we need to show that there exists a real number $x$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+5x+6<0.\n$$\n\nFinding a counterexample is sometimes a nontrivial task, but we only need one. In this case, substituting $x=-2.5$ suffices:\n\nBy substituting $x=-2.5$ into the expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+5x+6 & =(-2.5)^{2}+5(-2.5)+6 \\\\  & =-0.25 \\\\  & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we state our conclusion:\n\nSo, $x=-2.5$ is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false."}]}
